<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sennacherib</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 705–681 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sennacherib was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/neo-assyrian-empire">Neo-Assyrian Empire</a> from 705 to 681 BCE, known for rebuilding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nineveh">Nineveh</a> as a magnificent capital. He fought repeated wars against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elam">Elam</a> and destroyed Babylon in 689 BCE. His harsh treatment of Babylon fed lasting resentment, and he was assassinated by his own sons.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sennacherib.jpg" alt="Sennacherib" width="307" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Timo Roller · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sanherib-tr-4271.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
